e of the social media  celebrity before celebrity figures might  have felt like they were up on this  pedestal untouchable and unreachable but  now some of the most influential figures  have never been more relatable more  seemingly in reach and thankfully the  author seems to be very in touch with  the modern landscape because social  media plays a massive part in many of  these stories i was pleasantly surprised  when i saw stories about people trying  to become successful youtubers and  instagrams and tick tocks because i was  like yeah yeah  now you're coming in my neck of the  woods it was surreal seeing a manga that  was basically centered around my career  and industry and coming from the inside  seeing these stories based around  influences and their culture  it does a [ __ ] great job alright i'm  about to go on a tangent that doesn't  seem like it has anything to do with  anything but trust me i do have a point  and it does relate back to this [ __ ]  manga all right here's a little secret i  really hope won't come back to bite me  in the ass in the future by admitting i  often wonder how i would handle  getting cancelled okay this is not to  [ __ ] say that i sit in front of a  mirror rehearsing how to say i've made a  severe and continuous  lapse in my judgment nor do i think  there's anything i've done which i'm  scared is gonna get exposed and i'm  gonna have to apologize about but as a  youtuber whose career is tied to my  online presence and image council  culture and how to properly manage that  has become a massive factor in my job it  can be something that ends careers or it  can be something that you brush off and  move on from but regardless no one is  immune to its effect no matter how much  you think someone is uncancelable let's  talk about apology videos for example if  you think about it apology video should  be a simple affair someone does  something wrong so they apologize and  then people forgive them or they don't  but nowadays people getting cancelled  and creative apologies have become so  commonplace that it's almost become a  cliche good apologies bad apologies over  time we've been exposed to the entire  [ __ ] spectrum so much so that you can  even say that there's even a [ __ ]  meta for youtuber apology videos that we  can break down parody and sometimes even  rank and that's because  apology videos aren't about being sorry  it's about winning back public favor  it's pr  even if the person is actually sorry  like if i had to make an apology video  regardless of if i was being genuine or  not it's actually irrelevant because all  that's important is about making you  believe that i'm being genuine and  unfortunately being genuine and trying  to convince a mass audience that you are  being genuine are two entirely different  things now this may seem like a strange  tangent to go on that may look like i  have a weird obsession about the thought  of getting cancelled but that's because  i was astonished when i saw oshinoko  dealing with this exact topic not only  does it portray what happens when you're  just flooded with hate comments that  puts you in this self-destructive loop  you can't escape from that gives you  this  suffocating feeling which i can never  truly describe in words to someone who  hasn't been in that same position but it  also addresses how fickle public opinion  can be and how easily it can sway and  even the tactics and strategies you can  use to sway it to your side and game the  system they have a full-on death note  style breakdown of the mechanics of  getting cancelled and how to uncancel  yourself and i was absolutely amazed  reading this because some of this stuff  was exactly the same stuff i've thought  about because that's just what the  ecosystem has become so the biggest  compliment i can give is that from  someone working on the other side of the  industry is that oshinoko was pretty  spot on with its portrayal he managed to  make a super compelling story arc